@tradition mending-day
// Mending day: every fourth Sunday (week 1 of the cycle: days 7, 35, 63...), afternoon, the junior common room and
// the laundry on Deck 4. Uniforms mended, buttons sewn, spare uniforms swapped. Zeke Torres hosts (he knits; his days
// off are at the weekend), so day 7, your first Sunday, is a gentle afternoon with your escort if you want it.
k: 458
title: Mending day
when: every 4 weeks sunday week 1
at: 14:00-15:30
min: 25
jitter: 30
where: 4 pool common-room
where: 4 room Laundry: laundry
hold: none
who: torres-zeke always, juniors 45%, everyone 15%
anim: talk
host: torres-zeke
from: torres-zeke
ties: decor mending-table
invite: host=torres-zeke odds=40% line="Mending day this afternoon. Bring anything with a hole in it. I'll bring tea."

== mail
- Mending day tomorrow, {time}, the junior common room. Bring torn sleeves, loose buttons and odd socks. There's tea, spare uniforms to swap, and I'll show anyone how to sew a button.

== ask
- Mending day this afternoon. My elbows are out again.   #funny
- I've got three loose buttons and no idea what to do about them.   #funny
- Mending day later. There's tea, and nobody rushes you.

== here
- Over, under, pull it through.
- Does this sleeve look right to you?   #funny
- Nobody will ever know it was torn.   #warm

== thanks
- You sit down with a needle and a torn cuff. By the end it's nearly straight, and you're very proud of it.   #warm

== chatter
- Zeke knitted me a scarf at mending day. It's very long.   #funny
- I swapped my old uniform at mending day. This one actually fits.
- Mending day is just tea with needles. I love it.   #warm
